{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": [
      "ESNext",
      "DOM",
      "DOM.Iterable"
    ],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "strict": false,
    "noImplicitAny": false,
    "types": [
      "node"
    ]
  },
  "include": [
    "src"
  ],
  // Documented checkJs exclusions (see SUGGESTIONS-LOG-DUNGEON-SCHOLAR.md,
  // "tsconfig.json excludes ALL test files..."). These are an INTENTIONAL,
  // documented type-coverage gap, not an oversight:
  //   - **/*.test.js(x): the Vitest/happy-dom test surface is deliberately kept
  //     out of the JSDoc typecheck to keep  fast and green; the
  //     tests still run under Vitest, which is their gate. A future test-inclusive
  //     pass would need @testing-library / vitest type coverage before it could go green.
  //   - src/sw.js: the service worker runs in a WebWorker global scope that this
  //     config's default DOM lib does not model, so it is excluded rather than
  //     mis-typed against DOM globals.
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "dist-web",
    "**/*.test.js",
    "**/*.test.jsx",
    "src/sw.js"
  ]
}
